      ],
      "extract": "\\label{introdha} Let $v$ be a prime, $G_v = \\GG(\\Q_v)$ and $K_v$ a maximal compact subgroup. The usual Hecke algebra at $v$, with coefficients in a (say finite) ring $S$, can be described as $ \\Hom_{S G_v} \\left( S[G_v/K_v], S[G_v/K_v] \\right).$ If in place of $\\Hom$ we use $\\Ext$ (see \\S \\ref{sec:dha} for more details) we get a graded extension, which we may call the ``local derived Hecke algebra'':",
      "extractCut": true
